# Store and check out every file byte-for-byte, with no end-of-line rewriting.
#
# Git on Windows defaults to core.autocrlf=true, which converts LF to CRLF when
# it writes files into your working tree. That would mean restoring an old
# version gives you a file that differs from the original on every single line.
# This project exists partly to make reverts exact, so that conversion is off.
* -text
